\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces From situation blindness to an applicability-aware response. \textbf  {a}, A supported appointment becomes stale after resignation. \textbf  {b}, retrieval and relevance alone do not require resolution of that transition. \textbf  {c}, situation engineering constructs a provenance-linked state, validates claim applicability and propagates unresolved variables into response policy. \textbf  {d}, SituationCatch-Bench isolates seven corresponding diagnostic axes.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:engineering-planes}{{1}{3}{From situation blindness to an applicability-aware response. \textbf {a}, A supported appointment becomes stale after resignation. \textbf {b}, retrieval and relevance alone do not require resolution of that transition. \textbf {c}, situation engineering constructs a provenance-linked state, validates claim applicability and propagates unresolved variables into response policy. \textbf {d}, SituationCatch-Bench isolates seven corresponding diagnostic axes}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{eq:contract}{{3}{3}{Situation Engineering framework}{equation.0.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Oracle-state diagnostic accuracy. Bars show exact action-and-answer accuracy of SCQA (given the oracle situation state) and three heuristic baselines on all $n=4{,}200$ generated items. The result demonstrates that the specified invariants are executable. It does not estimate end-to-end LLM accuracy because situation variables are supplied rather than inferred. All systems are deterministic, so repeated runs give identical values; no error bars are shown because items share template families and are not independent samples (Methods).}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:accuracy}{{2}{5}{Oracle-state diagnostic accuracy. Bars show exact action-and-answer accuracy of SCQA (given the oracle situation state) and three heuristic baselines on all $n=4{,}200$ generated items. The result demonstrates that the specified invariants are executable. It does not estimate end-to-end LLM accuracy because situation variables are supplied rather than inferred. All systems are deterministic, so repeated runs give identical values; no error bars are shown because items share template families and are not independent samples (Methods)}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Accuracy by diagnostic category. Bars show exact action-and-answer accuracy of each system within each category ($n=600$ items per category). Each category isolates one applicability variable, enabling mechanism-level failure localization. Values are deterministic; no error bars are shown (Methods).}}{6}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:category}{{3}{6}{Accuracy by diagnostic category. Bars show exact action-and-answer accuracy of each system within each category ($n=600$ items per category). Each category isolates one applicability variable, enabling mechanism-level failure localization. Values are deterministic; no error bars are shown (Methods)}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Oracle-state component ablations. Bars show SCQA exact action-and-answer accuracy on all $n=4{,}200$ items when one state variable is removed (`none' is the intact system). Each removal produces exactly 300 errors, all in the category whose variable was removed. Values are deterministic; no error bars are shown (Methods).}}{7}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ablation}{{4}{7}{Oracle-state component ablations. Bars show SCQA exact action-and-answer accuracy on all $n=4{,}200$ items when one state variable is removed (`none' is the intact system). Each removal produces exactly 300 errors, all in the category whose variable was removed. Values are deterministic; no error bars are shown (Methods)}{figure.4}{}}
