\newlabel{tab:e8-stats}{{3}{25}{E8a free-tier replication accuracy (NVIDIA, rednote hi lab and Recursive models; Flint runs with minimal reasoning, whose tokens are included) (\%; $n=210$ items, 30 per category) with 95\% cluster-bootstrap confidence intervals (categories as clusters; 3000 resamples), the paired situation$-$structured contrast, and cost. A contrast interval that excludes zero is a directional estimate only within this bounded analysis}{table.ED.3}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Retrieval-augmented (RAG), full-evidence prompting, and a tool-using agent, mean accuracy over the three Gemini models on the $n=210$ sample. RAG answers from the top-3 lexically retrieved claims, which for these items are all of the item's claims as plain text in time order without timestamps or other metadata; Structured and Situation see all claims with their metadata; Agent may issue its own search queries over the item's claims before answering. Descriptively, on the two categories that most require reasoning over the applicability state -- temporal validity and observer knowledge -- the full-evidence conditions score above both retrieval and the agent; this category-level pattern is exploratory, and none of the retrieval-, prompt-, or tool-based interventions dominates overall.}}{25}{table.ED.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:e5-rag}{{4}{25}{Retrieval-augmented (RAG), full-evidence prompting, and a tool-using agent, mean accuracy over the three Gemini models on the $n=210$ sample. RAG answers from the top-3 lexically retrieved claims, which for these items are all of the item's claims as plain text in time order without timestamps or other metadata; Structured and Situation see all claims with their metadata; Agent may issue its own search queries over the item's claims before answering. Descriptively, on the two categories that most require reasoning over the applicability state -- temporal validity and observer knowledge -- the full-evidence conditions score above both retrieval and the agent; this category-level pattern is exploratory, and none of the retrieval-, prompt-, or tool-based interventions dominates overall}{table.ED.4}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Retrieval-augmented (RAG), full-evidence prompting, and a tool-using agent, mean accuracy over the three open-weight E6 models (Meta, DeepSeek, Qwen) on the $n=210$ sample. RAG answers from the top-3 lexically retrieved claims, which for these items are all of the item's claims as plain text in time order without timestamps or other metadata; Structured and Situation see all claims with their metadata; Agent may issue its own search queries over the item's claims before answering. Pre-registered scoring. Without timestamps, temporal accuracy falls to 34.4\% (23--50\% per model) against 100\% with them, as in E5. The Structured column is lowered by a scoring artefact for one model, whose prose-wrapped or boolean JSON answers the extractor misses (Methods); category comparisons are exploratory.}}{26}{table.ED.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:e6-rag}{{5}{26}{Retrieval-augmented (RAG), full-evidence prompting, and a tool-using agent, mean accuracy over the three open-weight E6 models (Meta, DeepSeek, Qwen) on the $n=210$ sample. RAG answers from the top-3 lexically retrieved claims, which for these items are all of the item's claims as plain text in time order without timestamps or other metadata; Structured and Situation see all claims with their metadata; Agent may issue its own search queries over the item's claims before answering. Pre-registered scoring. Without timestamps, temporal accuracy falls to 34.4\% (23--50\% per model) against 100\% with them, as in E5. The Structured column is lowered by a scoring artefact for one model, whose prose-wrapped or boolean JSON answers the extractor misses (Methods); category comparisons are exploratory}{table.ED.5}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Retrieval-augmented (RAG) and full-evidence prompting, mean accuracy over the three free-tier E8a models (NVIDIA, rednote hi lab, Recursive) on the $n=210$ sample. RAG answers from the top-3 lexically retrieved claims, which for these items are all of the item's claims as plain text in time order without timestamps or other metadata; Structured and Situation see all claims with their metadata. Pre-registered H2: temporal accuracy without metadata is below structured temporal accuracy in each model (50.0--56.7\% versus 96.7--100\%; per-model values in \texttt  {paper/results/e8\_rag\_by\_model.json}).}}{26}{table.ED.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:e8-rag}{{6}{26}{Retrieval-augmented (RAG) and full-evidence prompting, mean accuracy over the three free-tier E8a models (NVIDIA, rednote hi lab, Recursive) on the $n=210$ sample. RAG answers from the top-3 lexically retrieved claims, which for these items are all of the item's claims as plain text in time order without timestamps or other metadata; Structured and Situation see all claims with their metadata. Pre-registered H2: temporal accuracy without metadata is below structured temporal accuracy in each model (50.0--56.7\% versus 96.7--100\%; per-model values in \texttt {paper/results/e8\_rag\_by\_model.json})}{table.ED.6}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces E7: LLMs as situation sensors on the $n=210$ E5 items. Every sensor receives only the query time, question and claim texts; its state is passed unchanged to the SCQA engine. End-to-end is exact action-and-answer accuracy (\%); the other columns are claim-level slot accuracy (\%), scored identically for all sensors. Claim texts state no times, so Time is unrecoverable by design.}}{27}{table.ED.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:e7-sensor}{{7}{27}{E7: LLMs as situation sensors on the $n=210$ E5 items. Every sensor receives only the query time, question and claim texts; its state is passed unchanged to the SCQA engine. End-to-end is exact action-and-answer accuracy (\%); the other columns are claim-level slot accuracy (\%), scored identically for all sensors. Claim texts state no times, so Time is unrecoverable by design}{table.ED.7}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces E8b: natural-text temporal questions (SituatedQA test split, $n=300$, 75 per date type; free model endpoints). Accuracy (\%) for the undated question (Undated), the dated question with the same prompt (Dated), and the structured and situation prompts on the dated question. Contrasts are paired differences in percentage points with 95\% bootstrap intervals clustered on the source question: situation$-$structured on all items (H1), and dated$-$undated on time-dependent items (H2, $n=225$) and on control items dated at the dataset's collection year (Ctrl, $n=75$).}}{27}{table.ED.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:e8-nl}{{8}{27}{E8b: natural-text temporal questions (SituatedQA test split, $n=300$, 75 per date type; free model endpoints). Accuracy (\%) for the undated question (Undated), the dated question with the same prompt (Dated), and the structured and situation prompts on the dated question. Contrasts are paired differences in percentage points with 95\% bootstrap intervals clustered on the source question: situation$-$structured on all items (H1), and dated$-$undated on time-dependent items (H2, $n=225$) and on control items dated at the dataset's collection year (Ctrl, $n=75$)}{table.ED.8}{}}
